# Deployment

Deployment means putting the app online so other users can access it.

Our project has two main parts:

```text
front
server
```

The frontend is Next.js.

The backend is Express.js.

## Simple Deployment Structure

```text
Frontend -> Vercel
Backend -> Railway, Render, Fly.io, or VPS
Database -> MongoDB Atlas, Postgres, or another hosted database
Vector DB -> Pinecone, Qdrant, Chroma, MongoDB Atlas Vector Search, or pgvector
```

Current project choice:

```text
Database and vector search -> PostgreSQL with pgvector
ORM -> Prisma
Frontend -> Next.js
Backend -> Express.js
```

## Environment Variables

Production needs environment variables.

Examples:

```env
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=5000
CLIENT_URL=https://your-frontend.com
CORS_ORIGINS=https://your-frontend.com
LLM_PROVIDER=github
GITHUB_TOKEN=your_secret_token
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://...
JWT_SECRET=your_jwt_secret
STORAGE_PROVIDER=postgres
```

Secrets should not be written in code.

They should live in the hosting platform environment settings.

## Frontend Deployment

The frontend needs to know the backend URL.

Example:

```env
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://your-backend.com/api
```

## Backend Deployment

The backend needs:

```text
model API keys
database URL
vector database URL
CORS origins
upload limits
```

## Deployment Checklist

```text
Frontend builds successfully
Backend starts successfully
Environment variables are set
Prisma migrations are applied
Prisma Client is generated
CORS allows the frontend domain
Uploads work
Indexing works
Chat works
Login/register works
Team invites work
Document sharing works
Activity logs work
Logs are visible
Secrets are not exposed
```

## Simple Presentation Version

```text
Deployment puts the frontend, backend, PostgreSQL/pgvector database, and model provider online. It also requires migrations, correct environment variables, CORS settings, and secret management.
```
